This is a Commodore dealer demo that ran on some A1200HD units set up for display purposes at the point of sale.

I believe this was an official demo released by Commodore, however I am aware that regions were mostly responsible for their own marketing - there are separate productions for France and Germany (which were already available) - so this one may be a Commodore Australia/NZ production. 

As a 14-year-old in early 1993 I used to watch this running on the display A1200 at my local department store and wish desperately that I could have one.

Nine years later I finally had my very own A1200, and after a 25-year search I now have the ability to play this demo on it!

Massive thanks to Nick Trounson and his friend Dean for getting it to me!

---

Installation:

- Must be installed to a HD on an A1200 (may also work on an A4000, but... why?)
	- either write out all 5 disks to floppies, or use an ADF mounting tool
	- run the installer on disk 1
	- choose the type of display you have
	- keep feeding it what it wants until it finishes
	- reboot the machine once it's done and it will start automatically every boot unless you hit ctrl-C first

Other notes:

- Looks like it was put together in AmigaVision
- It's supposed to loop, but it crashes pretty regularly on my 060-accelerated A1200 - disabling CPU caches lets it run for longer without crashing but doesn't completely resolve the issue. Would likely run a lot better with a vanilla copy of WB 3.x

Enjoy :)